  "status_text": "For every graph it is now checked that even a circuit allowed NOT gates needs about one gate for each row and each column outside the largest group of identical ones. An AND/OR/NOT circuit representing an n by m graph has at least (n - a) + (m - b) - 1 gates, where a and b are its largest groups of equal rows and of equal columns [L-meta-19361]. It is a floor of reading, below the number of inputs, and it lets every circuit with NOT gates be measured against a checked row before it is posted.",
